<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no" ?>
<FinalDraft DocumentType="Script" Template="No" Version="1">

  <Content>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <SceneProperties Length="3 1/8" Page="1" Title=""/>
      <Text>Int. Apartment - Day</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Chaz sits with his dad, Bill 59, on the couch.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Chaz</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Dad, I’m going to learn how to ride a motorcycle.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Bill perks up.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Bill</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Oh?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Chaz stammers slightly as he attempts to fill the silent air  with the ‘why’ before its overtaken with the ‘why not.’</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>CHAZ</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>It’s something I’ve had an interest in for a long time. I’ve had this nagging dream of driving up the coast on highway one, along the ocean.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Bill slinks back down in his posture.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>BILL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>But it’s dangerous? Aren’t you afraid of what could happen?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>CHAZ</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Yes, I am afraid of that. But I have a larger fear of what wouldn’t happen if I didn’t try.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Chaz leans forward and places a hand on Bills shoulder.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>CHAZ (CONT’D)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I understand your reservation. I can imagine the fear of a child pursuing a dangerous hobby, but I have faith in me, I only ask the same from you.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Bill maintains his reserved position on it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Bill</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>It’s not just that you’re my child. I can’t stand idly by as someone I love endangers himself.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Chaz, slightly defensive.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>CHAZ</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Methane leaks. Radon. Saturated fat. Tainted spinach. Attacks, both foreign and domestic. </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Bill perks up.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>BILL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Yeah, yeah...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>CHAZ</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Life is conflict. Death is inevitable. Why not have some fun while we’re here? Why not try something new while I’m still young and strong and capable? </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>BILL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>You could get hurt.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>CHAZ</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Is it wrong for me to say that, maybe that’s part of why I want to attempt it? It requires skill. A skill I don’t have. I want to learn something new. I want to grow.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>BILL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>But...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>CHAZ</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I want to feel free, uninhibited, vulnerable. I want that. Every reason you present to me as why I shouldn’t, those are on my list of why I should, plus more!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>BILL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Look, I can’t stop you. You’re a grown man and can do as you wish, just know that your father protests.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>CHAZ</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>And, I don’t take that lightly. I know you’d rather I didn’t. But, you rode your bicycle to work for many years, you’ve given me that bike not long ago.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>BILL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>But that’s a bicycle, that’s different.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>CHAZ</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>And I’d say that riding a bicycle is more dangerous than a motorbike.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>BILL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>How?!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>CHAZ</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>You ride in the street but you don’t get a lane. Cars whizz by with little regard for the cyclist. I’m rarely granted the luxury of a bike lane, and still I have to worry about people pulling out of businesses with no regard of cyclists.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>BILL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>True.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>CHAZ</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>With a motorbike. I’m in traffic. I’m allowed a full lane. I don’t plan on splitting lanes, I just plan to flow with traffic as if I were a car. I have proper lights and signals. Aside from the speed differential, motor bikes are far safer.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>BILL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>But the speed difference is huge.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>CHAZ</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Look. I’ve been hit on my bicycle by a car. It’s no fun, I was injured worse than I’d ever been. But, let’s not forget the drunk driver in Wisconsin...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>BILL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>And if you were on a motorcycle you’d have been killed!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>CHAZ</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>And if I was on a bicycle I wouldn't? Look, life is risk.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>BILL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>A calculated risk.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>CHAZ</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>It’s a risk based on doing what you enjoy or fearing your own shadow and waiting to die.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>BILL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Don’t be so dramatic.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>CHAZ</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I choose to </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="">live...come</Text>
      <Text> what may.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text></Text>
    </Paragraph>
  </Content>

